                                <li>On the settings page, scroll down to the "Your apps" section.</li>
                                <li>If you don't have a web app, click "Add app" and choose the Web icon (<span className="font-bold">&lt;/&gt;</span>).</li>
                                <li>Follow the instructions until you reach the "Add Firebase SDK" step, where you will find the <span className="font-bold">Firebase config object</span> that starts with <code className="bg-gray-100 p-1 rounded font-mono text-xs dark:bg-gray-600 dark:text-gray-200">const firebaseConfig = &#123; ... &#125;</code>.</li>
                                <li>Copy only the object <code className="bg-gray-100 p-1 rounded font-mono text-xs dark:bg-gray-600 dark:text-gray-200">&#123; ... &#125;</code> (make sure to copy the curly braces &#123;&#125;) and paste it into the text box below.</li>
                                <li>Click "Save Firebase Config".</li>
                            </ol>
                            <label htmlFor="firebase-config" className="block text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 mb-1 dark:text-gray-200">Firebase Config (JSON Object)</label>
